.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt VEB 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm veb ,
.Nm vport
.Nd Virtual Ethernet Bridge pseudo network device
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To compile this driver into the kernel,
place the following line in your
kernel configuration file:
.Bd -ragged -offset indent
.Cd "device veb"
.Ed
.Pp
Alternatively, to load the driver as a
module at boot time, place the following line in
.Xr loader.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
if_veb_load="YES"
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver provides a Layer 2 Ethernet bridge for virtual network
topologies such as
.Xr bhyve 8
VMs and VNET
.Xr jail 8 Ns s .
As opposed to
.Xr bridge 4 ,
it does not support the Spanning Tree Protocol,
.Xr pfil 9
packet filtering, or implicit host membership.
.Pp
Each
.Nm
interface is created at runtime using interface cloning.
This is most easily done with the
.Xr ifconfig 8
.Cm create
command or using the
.Va cloned_interfaces
variable in
.Xr rc.conf 5 .
.Nm vport
interfaces are created the same way.
The
.Nm
can be configured via
.Xr netlink 4
using
.Xr ifconfig 8 .
.Ss Host presence
The
.Nm
interface has no host presence.
It cannot be assigned any
.Xr inet 4
or
.Xr inet6 4
address, it does not deliver frames to the host network stack, and it
does not transmit frames originating from the host.
.Pp
To connect the host to a
.Nm ,
create a
.Nm vport
interface and add it to the
.Nm
as a port.
A
.Nm vport
acts as an ordinary Ethernet interface to the host;
addresses assigned to it are reachable from other ports, and traffic
the host transmits is forwarded by the
.Nm .
Addresses can only be assigned to a
.Nm vport
while it is a port of a
.Nm .
A
.Nm
can have at most one
.Nm vport ,
and a
.Nm vport
can be a port of only one
.Nm
at any given time.
.Ss Ports
Ethernet and
.Xr vlan 4
interfaces can be added to the
.Nm
as ports.
An interface can be a port of only one
.Nm
and cannot be a port or member of both a
.Nm
and a
.Xr bridge 4
at the same time.
A
.Xr vlan 4
interface whose parent is a
.Xr bridge 4
or a
.Nm
cannot be added.
.Pp
An interface must not have an IPv4 address when it is added.
On addition, if the interface has an IPv6 link-local address, all of its
IPv6 addresses are removed and a message is logged.
The interface is then placed into promiscuous mode and isolated from
the host network stack:
no addresses can be assigned to it and its capabilities cannot be
changed.
Promiscuous mode and capabilities are restored when the port is
removed.
.Pp
The MTU of a
.Nm
is set by the first port that is added to it.
All subsequent ports are set to that MTU.
If the MTU of a
.Nm
is changed, every port of that
.Nm
is adjusted to match.
The MTU of any port, including a
.Nm vport ,
cannot be changed directly while being a port.
.Pp
The TOE, TSO, TXCSUM, TXCSUM_IPV6, and MEXTPG capabilities remain
enabled on the ports only if every port has them enabled.
LRO is always disabled on the ports.
Because the
.Nm vport
supports none of the transmit offloads, adding a
.Nm vport
disables them on all ports.
.Ss Forwarding
Just like
.Xr bridge 4 ,
the
.Nm
learns the source address of each frame it receives, indexed by
Ethernet address and VLAN ID.
Unicast frames destined for a known address are only forwarded out the
port on which that address was learned;
broadcast and multicast frames are forwarded to all other ports.
Unicast frames destined for an unknown address are forwarded to all
other ports with the
.Li DISCOVER
flag set.
Frames addressed to the reserved IEEE 802.1D group addresses
.Li 01:80:c2:00:00:00
to
.Li 01:80:c2:00:00:0f
are not forwarded.
VLAN tags are passed through unaltered as the
.Nm
currently has no VLAN filtering capability.
If a port is the parent of a
.Xr vlan 4
interface, all VLAN-tagged frames received on that port are passed to
.Xr vlan 4
rather than being forwarded by the veb.
By default, the address cache holds 2000 entries, and an entry expires 1200
seconds after the last frame from that address is seen.
A sweep removes all expired entries every 300 seconds.
Both values can be configured per
.Nm .
Static entries do not expire.
.Pp
Each port has the following flags.
Newly added ports have
.Li LEARNING
and
.Li DISCOVER
set automatically.
.Bl -tag -width "DISCOVER"
.It Li LEARNING
Learn source addresses from frames received on the port.
.It Li DISCOVER
Receive copies of unicast frames to unknown addresses.
.It Li STICKY
Addresses learned on the port do not expire and do not move to another
port.
.It Li PRIVATE
Do not forward frames between this port and any other
.Li PRIVATE
port.
.It Li VPORT
Read-only; set on the port that is the
.Nm Ns 's
.Nm vport .
.El
.Pp
The link state of a
.Nm
is up when at least one port other than the
.Nm vport
has link, or when the
.Nm
has ports but none of them, besides the
.Nm vport ,
reports a link state.
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va net.link.veb.log_mac_flap
Log a message when an address moves between ports.
Defaults to 1.
.El
